lso how the story manages to tie back  into the beginning or an earlier part of  the story to help  grant a greater sense of occasion  gravity or  meaning to the conflict at hand i like  to think back to series like one piece  or even dragon ball  one piece is filled to bursting with  conclusions tying themselves back to the  beginning or an earlier part of the arc  to better inform its conclusion  think of the going mary saving everyone  from any's lobby or  think the giant shadow and fight with a  nel in skypia and think of the battle  that luffy had with katakuri that was  perfectly informed by the ark in  question and kanakuri's relationship  with his family this tells us something  about the world it tells us something  about why they're fighting and it tells  us something about the characters  none of this is random and it makes the  conclusion all the more satisfying  because of it it feels more real  similarly when it came to gohan  transforming during his fight with cell  we knew and felt that this was a  monumental moment because  it like everything else i've mentioned  was built up to  and when it happened it did so with  great occasion and fanfare much to the  delight of  everyone watching but when requiem gold  experience took out diavolo  the boss of the massive criminal  syndicate i felt like i watched an  ending that was put together by someone  that hadn't read or known anything about  the prior events of the story  because it didn't really tie anything  together granted i appreciate that the  bow and arrow stuff has been part of the  story since part four  but the elements that this arrow  contributes to the story have nothing to  do with anything we've learned about it  before other than what the arrow looks  like  the concept of piercing your own stand  isn't introduced until the third  act of this arc which is all in service  of ending this arc the way araki wanted  to but if he wanted to  why not make that aspect part of the  beginning the way iraqi wanted to end  this arc is by granting gold experience  not giorno  gold experience a power-up that gives  the stand agency and a brand new ability  that perfectly fits the situation to  take out diavolo  it has nothing to do with journal  nothing to do with what jorno has  learned or achieved throughout this  journey feels as though it's contributed  in any meaningful way towards this  ending and as a result  i feel like a new random character in  requiem gold experience just shows up  with a brand new convenient power  to save the day this more than anything  made the ending fall flat for me  causing me to wonder where the tension  went and what was the point of this  entire journey for me the best part of  this particular story is  everything that happened up until the  point they meet polymorph in the  coliseum which was wonderful to see and  his transformation into the tortoise was  fittingly hilarious too  however unfortunately this isn't where  the ending concludes either when diavolo  is defeated by not giorno but instead  his stand gold experience  we are shown something of a miniark that  takes place  over two episodes wherein we see a  flashback showing what bruno and mista  did right before meeting giorno in  person towards the beginning of the  story this was one of the strangest  decisions made  narratively in my opinion right as the  climax hits we are dragged back in time  to the beginning of the story for what  feels like an ova with optional content  killing what little hype and expectation  i had during the occasion  in favor of showing me a story about  fate told through a boulder with  separation anxiety  all before calling back to the main  story where everyone just sort of says  goodbye  and good job to each other and walks off  before once again cutting to the future  with  giorno as a mob boss for a few seconds  what  happened to the people of naples he  wanted to help what happened to what  bruno wanted to achieve for his town  what happened to giorno's goal and are  we meant to just accept that everything  is fine and that he took care of it  off-screen  these are the motivating factors that  caused us to get behind these characters  in the first place  showing what the character has achieved  is part of the payoff it's the goal of  the entire story this is like watching  ash ketchum travel far and wide to  become the pokemon league champion only  for the writers to cut that part out  this would be like watching luffy have  the heartfelt confrontation with nami  during arlen park  only for them to cut out the gang  fighting arlong and flash to the  aftermath for three or four  seconds having spent months covering the  story one thing i've become accustomed  to  has been how these stories like to bask  in the spoils of their win  and the extravagant means with which  they like to conclude the final fights  but moreover i like how the main  characters play a role in that finish  but giorno really doesn't get to do much  of anything other than to facilitate the  existence of  gold experiences change i've spent a  long time talking about these hang-ups  i've had because i wanted to make  perfectly clear that these issues i have  are aspects of the story i've attempted  to think through i've no issue with this  being someone's favorite ending and i've  been diligent  in saying that these are just my own  personal opinions but by the time i  reached the ending of the story i was  completely convinced that this wasn't so  much an act but more so  the story of how jorno became who he is  or should i say the story about how  giorno  looked like he was the one who was going  to achieve something only for gold  experience to actually be the one to do  that instead  maybe gold experience should be the mob  boss now in other words  this story didn't feel like it was in  service of its own narrative but instead  it felt like it was in service of the  next and  when it comes to the conclusion of a  particular arc i don't care about the  next one i care about what we've built  up to here and now and for me golden  wind didn't deliver  anything that i wanted personally now  okay that's a lot of negativity  with all of that said however 95 of this  story is by far  my favorite arc in the story with  characters that felt  fun and relatable i'm still a firm  believer that bruno mister and naranja  are  the best characters in the story heck  the globe diavolo got in the second half  made him one of the more interesting  characters too  which brings me to this moment it's time  for the tier list over the last eight  videos and two months i have reviewed  all five currently released and  localized arcs  of hirohiko araki's jojo's bizarre  adventure an anthology of stories  following primarily the bloodlines of  the joe stars and in the case of the  most recent arc  dio brando however seeing as this will  be my last review  i make on jojo until part six gets  translated i will  right here and now present you all with  my tier list for my favorite jojo's  and my favorite jojo ops alright so  right off the bat i'm gonna need to  destroy  everything from d tier and below  everything on this list i at the very  least  enjoyed particularly with the music i  even had all of these tracks playing  while i worked on this video and yes  i know all of the lyrics see tier  jonathan joestar  so working our way up starting with the  jojo that initiated this whole journey  we have the og himself  jonathan joster as the original jojo he  sort of sets the standard and  to be frank had you approached me before  i began this review and told me i would  end up  liking jonathan i never would have  believed you while not being very  interesting in terms of personality i  found his virtuous death both  tragic and shocking made all the more  emotional in later installments  particularly in their ops  but i'll get to that later next up  traitor's requiem  it's funny how the first jojo and the  last song from part 5  are opening up this list traitor's  requiem is a somewhat understated song  and one that i truthfully almost forgot  to include on this list maybe i'd rank  it higher if it had more time to grow on  me however  as the second op from golden wind it'll  have to stand alongside jonathan as the  bar  set for this series chase coming in as a  sea tier entrant is  chase from diamond is unbreakable as the  middle child of the three diamond is  unbreakable ops  it didn't really have much narratively  to play with from a visual perspective  and musically i think this is probably  one of the songs i listen to the least  with that said i still know all of the  lyrics and i do love it  b-tier giorno giovanna and with that we  arrive at the tier labeled bee  and i get a sinking feeling people are  going to be really upset that i've  decided to place jorno here  as you've seen in this and the last  review covering the events of part 5 i  am a massive fan of what it managed to  achieve in captivating me but also  in demonstrating how much better araki  managed to get as a writer during his  time  working on jojo with all of that said  due to the ensemble nature of this story  and the lack of screen time  journal ultimately received i didn't  really have that much of a chance to  form much of a bond with him as a  character there are plenty of instances  throughout enduring the story where i  really enjoyed him as a character  however it wasn't enough to give him an  edge over the other jojo's on this tier  list for me  fighting gold on the other hand i have  no idea as to whether or not placing  fighting gold on the b  tier is a controversial take or not  seeing this song here shouldn't be an  indication of anything other than the  quality and high standard all of the  other tracks have set  but yeah i really like this song just  not as much as i've come to expect from  jojo  it could have something to do with the  chorus but who knows bloody stream  like i said i had no idea if the  previous one was a controversial take  i do however know for a fact that this  one will be controversial  bloody stream i adore the song and i  love how cool and smooth the lead  singer's vocals are  i have no idea if this song's proximity  to other tracks in the series played a  role or whether or not  it's much more subdued arrangement when  compared with the others played into its  position here  i just never really connected with the  song in the same intense way i did with  all the others that came after on this  list  as b tier goes i'd say this is the  strongest contender for a tier but  not quite i had to draw the line  somewhere in the sand and  bloody stream just didn't make the cut  for me personally  a tier crazy noisy bizarre town i'm a  massive fan of tracks that capture the  essence and tone of their respective  stories  and if i'm being perfectly honest crazy  noisy bizarre town sets the standard in  that department catchy upbeat with  fittingly bizarre visuals featured over  the quaint little town the story is  based within  this is perhaps more than any other an  earworm i'll never shake  and you know what i'm not even mad  josuke hikashikata  something i've noticed in my reading  through of jojo's bizarre adventure is  that the main characters seem to take  more and more of a backseat role from  joseph onwards and  while josuke didn't get the giorno  treatment in that he had to totally  share with all of the other side  characters  equally i felt like i could have done  with more screen time with josuke there  really aren't too many scenes in that  story where the audience gets to spend  some one-on-one time with josuke  and i think that probably played a role  into my bonding with the character  i feel like josuke deserves to be on the  s tier but for some reason i felt like  after the arc finished there was  still so much i wanted to know and learn  about josuke i wanted more  which i suppose is a good thing if not  for the fact that i expected more  regardless from what i did see i saw a  subtly emotional light-hearted and  relaxed jojo that i  thoroughly enjoyed from start to finish  and for a long time was in the running  for my all-time  favorite jojo kujo jotaro unlike josuke  whom i liked from the outset jodoro was  very much a character that took time to  grow on me initially my exposure to him  via the anime many many years ago  created a feeling  of boredom surrounding the character  however through the manga i sincerely  thought a lot more subtle emotional cues  shine through  that coupled with some wonderfully timed  straight face gags and some  truly badass scenes with him journal  climbs out of the expectations i had and  into the extremely entertaining a-tier  great days of all the tracks on this  list this is the one that surprised me  the most by how much i love it capping  off the last spot on  a tier is diamond is unbreakable's op  great days  this track managed to reach this high  spot despite me only knowing about it  for the last few weeks  which i mean speaks volumes about how  much i like and listen to this  song it's not as punchy as some of the  other tracks in s tier but as far as the  softer jojo tracks go this one is my  absolute favorite crazy noisy bizarre  town is awesome  but i'd sincerely think i enjoyed this  one just that little bit more  and now the time you've all been waiting  for time for the s  tier first up sono chi no kyoku  kicking things off and setting the  standard from this point on is the last  op of part three  sonochino unlike many of the other ops  this one in particular feels as though  it's mirroring the story starting  ominously it builds to an impactful  moment following the visuals of the  stardust crusaders making their way to  dio and man when they do eventually get  to dio this op  features a revised do edit mirroring the  story perfectly and giving further  context to the original version it's  catchy  it's informed by the story 